--- a/docs/research/architecture-decisions.md
+++ b/docs/research/architecture-decisions.md
@@ -337,3 +337,11 @@ uses its FinalizationRegistry cleanup on supported runtimes, and offers idempote
 entering WASM. No cache can evict a live prepared codec, and the object is neither
 cloneable nor transferable across instances/workers. Prepared methods retain all
 numeric, phrase, range and error contracts of the stateless methods.
+
+## Bounded prepared batches
+
+The prepared facade supports ordered, all-or-throw encode/decode arrays capped at
+4096 elements. Rust validates each item in order; JS invalid-input markers preserve
+precedence across syntax and range errors. A separate batchIndex identifies the
+item while position retains the unknown word index. The transport uses wasm-bindgen
+externref arrays, without custom delimiter framing or public raw handles.
